@startuml backup-run
title scripts/backup.sh : one cold backup, read from left to right

skinparam dpi 110
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ConditionStyle diamond
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #555555
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF4D6
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #B8860B
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #999999
skinparam SwimlaneTitleFontStyle bold

|#FAFAFA|1. Check\ncontainers still up|
start
if (Run as root, **backup.conf** there\nand naming the archives folder?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:Refuse and leave
  Nothing is stopped,
  nothing is reported;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (Another backup already running?) then (yes)
  :Nothing done;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:Take the lock
A run that was interrupted left
its log behind: report it;
if (**rsync**, **tar** and **docker**\navailable?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:**2.2** Containers **not** stopped
  **send-alert.sh** mails
  which tool is missing;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (Volumes folder found,\n**.env** and **INSTALL_INFO.txt** there,\narchives folder outside the volumes?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:**2.2** Containers **not** stopped
  **send-alert.sh** mails what is
  missing or misplaced;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Measure what will be copied:
volumes/ + .env + INSTALL_INFO.txt;
if (Room for the staging copy\n**and** the future tar.gz?\n(twice that size, plus 10 %)) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:**2.2** Containers **not** stopped
  **send-alert.sh** mails the alert address;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (Staging folder made?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:Containers **not** stopped
  The run ends in error, no mail;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

|#FFF3E0|2.1 Outage\ncontainers down|
#FFE2B8:Stop the containers of this project,
all together;
#FFE2B8:**Copy with rsync to the staging folder:**
* the folder **volumes/**
* the file **.env**
* the file **INSTALL_INFO.txt**;
note right
  **What is copied, and nothing else**
  volumes/ : database, mailboxes,
  DKIM keys, queues, rspamd, redis
  .env : every setting and secret
  INSTALL_INFO.txt : the install record
end note
#FFE2B8:Start the containers again,
copy done or not;
note right
  A run interrupted while they are
  down starts them again before leaving
end note
if (Every container UP?\n(running and healthy,\nwithin 3 minutes)) then (no)
  #FFE2B8:Start them once more
  and wait again;
  if (Every container UP now?) then (no)
    if (manager-api UP?\n(send-alert.sh goes through it)) then (yes)
      #FFD9D9:**send-alert.sh** names
      the containers still down
      (best effort);
    else (no)
      #FFD9D9:**No mail possible**
      the alert needs the server
      that is down;
    endif
    #FFD9D9:Keep the failure as a report
    for the manager, exit in error;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
else (yes)
endif
if (Copy done without error?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:The server is back up
  **send-alert.sh**: the copy failed
  No archive is made, exit in error;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

|#FAFAFA|3. Compress\nserver up|
:tar.gz of the staging copy
(volumes/ + .env + INSTALL_INFO.txt)
backup-YYYY-MM-DD.tar.gz,
made in the staging folder;
if (Archive made?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:**send-alert.sh**: the archive
  could not be made
  Staging folder deleted, exit in error;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

|#F1F8F1|4. Store|
if (Archive moved to **BACKUP_DIR**\nof backup.conf?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:Staging folder deleted
  The run ends in error, no mail;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
#D9F2D9:Delete the staging folder;
note right
  One archive per day: a second run
  on the same day replaces
  the archive of that day
end note

|#F1F8F1|5. Off-site\nif set|
if (**BACKUP_OFFSITE** set?\n(user@host:/path)) then (no)
else (yes)
  :Send the archive with
  **rsync over ssh**, nothing else;
  if (Sent?) then (no)
    #FFD9D9:Archive kept here
    **send-alert.sh**, result "partial"
    No rotation;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  if (Box "delete here\nonce sent" ticked?) then (yes)
    #D9F2D9:Delete the archive here;
  else (no)
    #D9F2D9:Keep it here too;
  endif
endif

|#FAFAFA|6. Rotation\nkeep N days, no more|
:Read **BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS**
(5 by default)
List the archives here and off-site;
note right
  One archive per day:
  5 days kept = 5 archives at most
  Runs only after a backup that worked
end note
while (Another archive\nto look at?) is (yes)
  if (Older than\nBACKUP_KEEP_DAYS days?) then (yes)
    #FFD9D9:Delete this archive;
  else (no)
    #D9F2D9:Keep this archive;
  endif
endwhile (no)

|#EEF3FB|7. Report, then\nleave only the archives|
:Put in one report the result,
the durations, the log of the run,
where the archives are, which exist
and which were deleted off-site
Delete **backup.log**;
note right
  backup.log and the staging copy
  only exist while the run lasts
  Every failure above ends here too,
  from the taking of the lock on
end note
:Send the report to the manager, by a
route only this machine can reach;
if (Manager answered?) then (yes)
  #D9F2D9:Taken: stored in the **database**,
  shown on the Backups page
  Refused as invalid: dropped
  Delete the report;
else (no)
  :Keep the report, the one file left,
  for a later run to deliver
  (the last 50 at most);
endif
#D9F2D9:The folder holds the archives
and nothing else;
stop
@enduml
